-- #846 (lane F, 2026-10-21): the Orgrimmar zeppelin towers in the travel graph (playerbots DB; beyond AC - AC's graph is 3.3.5 data).
--
-- Root cause: since 4.0 the four Orgrimmar zeppelins (Thundercaller 164871, Iron Eagle 175080, Mighty Wind 186238, The Zephyr
-- 190549) dock at towers that are reached by the three Orgrimmar elevators 206608 / 206609 / 206610 (static type-11
-- transports, `gameobject` guids 187462 / 187461 / 187463; TransportAnimation 5.4.8: +66.45 / +61.30 / +66.91 yd, 4.1-5.4 s
-- pauses at each landing). The tower tops are a separate navmesh component on purpose (4545 polys: the three upper landings
-- and the four zeppelin decks), exactly like the Thunder Bluff mesas, which AC's graph crosses with Mesa Elevator 4170 /
-- 4171 / 11898 / 11899 links. The graph had no elevator nodes here, and 2026_10_15_00.sql had to leave the four tower docks
-- (1941 1944 1981 2035) with transport links only, so no roaming bot could ever walk to an Orgrimmar zeppelin.
--
-- Fix, following the Mesa Elevator rows (nodes 1867/1868, links type 3 object 4170 extra_cost 5 down / 15 up, 2 path points):
--  - 6 nodes: each elevator's bottom landing (the spawn = TransportAnimation frame 0) and top landing (spawn + the top frame);
--  - 6 elevator links (type 3) between them;
--  - walk links (type 1) from every top landing to every tower dock, and from every bottom landing to the Orgrimmar ground
--    nodes 426 2091 1713 488 (537 and 847 are not reachable on this navmesh). Paths: offline Detour A* over the 5.4.8 mmaps
--    (mmaps 0001_*.mmtile), resampled every 10 yd; the
--    landing point is the navmesh poly 8.5-16 yd from the shaft centre on the landing's own level (off the platform footprint),
--    a dock's land point is the nearest tower-deck poly within 35 yd of the zeppelin stop at deck level (+-3 yd).
-- All rows are linked / calculated = 1, so TravelNodeMap::LoadOrGenerate does not regenerate or re-save the graph.
-- Undo: DELETE FROM playerbots_travelnode WHERE id BETWEEN 3780 AND 3785; and the same node ids in _link / _path (node_id or to_node_id).



